		{
			"id": "fWaMFiv9",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -325.951171875,
			"y": -161.5078125,
			"width": 693,
			"height": 250,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "#d0bfff",
			"fillStyle": "hachure",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "aAV",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 110186682,
			"version": 986,
			"versionNonce": 2108106234,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1772645292091,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Clock drift is the gradual divergence of a machine’s clock from\nreal time due to hardware imperfections.\n\nAll hardware clocks rely on quartz oscillators.\nThey are not perfectly accurate.\n\nTypical drift:\n10–100 ppm (parts per million)\n\nThat’s several milliseconds per second",
			"rawText": "Clock drift is the gradual divergence of a machine’s clock from real time due to hardware imperfections.\n\nAll hardware clocks rely on quartz oscillators.\nThey are not perfectly accurate.\n\nTypical drift:\n10–100 ppm (parts per million)\n\nThat’s several milliseconds per second",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "center",
			"verticalAlign": "middle",
			"containerId": "rcUtXhOx",
			"originalText": "Clock drift is the gradual divergence of a machine’s clock from real time due to hardware imperfections.\n\nAll hardware clocks rely on quartz oscillators.\nThey are not perfectly accurate.\n\nTypical drift:\n10–100 ppm (parts per million)\n\nThat’s several milliseconds per second",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
		{
			"id": "9H41qFECIB9RPZ-JII8lj",
			"type": "rectangle",
			"x": -336.3691406250001,
			"y": 115.33203125,
			"width": 720.4843750000002,
